NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1044,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,4,2,3,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":2.9387,"rank":0.0523,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV001201","role":"target","render":{"description":"Predictions that a sick man will recover, will plough first with a white horse and later with a black horse, and that the black horse will pull the hearse, come true. The horses first harnessed to the hearse refuse, so the black horse has to be harnessed.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43204","original":"Voorloop. \nSchoenmaker vertelt.\n\nOal Kamies noast ons was de haile winter al aon 't sukkeln.\n't Gung dan veur-, dan achteroet,\nBuurman Wessels was 't er op 'n dag hèn west te kieken, hou d' oale 't muik.\n\"Kamies gait achteroet, hai hoal 't nich meer,\" zee hai.\nMoar opa, oal Steffen, zee.\n\"Nee Wessels, Kamies wordt weer beter.\nHai hef nou 'n wit peerd. En 't volgend veurjoar plougt hai 't land mit 'n zwaarde. \nDat zwaarde peerd brengt hum vot.\" \n't Widde wör verkoft en 'n zwaarde kwam d'r veur in de ploats.\nEen buurman hef hiermit de grond pluigd.\nVolgende zömmer störf Kamies.\nVeur de woagen zol 'n peerd van de buren.\nKamies zien aigen har er nog nooit veur west en doarum wol ze hom laiver nich broeken. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV000905","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Before there is a road, the sound of a dog cart and the barking of dogs is heard.","place":"Ter Apel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43087","original":"Maar wel is het waar, dat veel mensen in het veen een hondekar hebben horen ratelen. Ook hoorden ze de hond blaffen.\nLang voor er een weg was en voor er later inderdaad een hondekar langs trok.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.87667,7.05972]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006906","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that one day many soldiers would come with wagons without horses. When the Canadians arrive in 1945, someone remembers this.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43580","original":"Veurloop.\nt Is n hail zet leden. Oabram zee es n moal: “Hier koomt nog ais n haile bult seldoatn. Ik zai ze bie t hoes van H. en bie K en op t haim van Z. Zai hebt woagens bie zuk zunder peerden.\n Toun in 1945 de Canadezen kwamen, was dr nog aine oale, dei zuk dat vertelsel van de spoukkieker in t zin schoot. Hai lag op berre en kun nait best wat zegn, omdat e verlamd was. \nMoar zoveul begreepn wie wel van zien “hoi, hoi”, dat e zegn wol:“Oabram zee t ja al?”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV008709","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Noise in the horse stable in the evening is an omen that a horse will kick something to pieces.","place":"Wessinghuizen","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45305","original":"t Gebeurde wol is, dat ze s oavends wat in t peerdstaal heurden. Kiekn deden ze maistied nich, man ze wuzzen wol, dat t peerd gauw wat stukn hou-en zol; door was t n veurbeduudsel van.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.0525,7.075]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessinghuizen.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2386,"rank":0.4673,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ051006","role":"member","render":{"description":"A father warns his children never to walk in the middle of the road at night. After all, they might run into a funeral procession.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25083","original":"Heit woe noait lije, dat wy froeger by jountiid of by nacht midden op 'e wei roannen. Sels gong er ek altyd yn 'e berm lâns. Men koe ris tsjin in lykwein oprinne, wie syn sizzen altyd.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2266","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"You were warned not to walk in the cart track or on the bridle path at night. Because there you could meet evil spirits.","place":"Heesselt","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127631","original":"Dat weet ik ook nog. Je werd gewaarschuwd om 's nachts niet in 't wagenspoor of in 't paardenpad te lopen. Want daar kon je de boze geesten tegenkomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ112406","role":"member","render":{"description":"Because funeral processions need the space, it is best not to walk in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/30112","original":"Noait mat men by nacht midden op 'e wei rinne, fanwegen in lykstaesje, dy't altyd paed ha mat en dy't dan wolris tsjin jin oanstompe kin.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ034606","role":"member","render":{"description":"You should never walk in the middle of the road, because you may be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22678","original":"Der woarde ús al hiel jong leard, noait midden op 'e wei to rinnen. Hwant it koe gebeure dat der in lykstaesje oankom en dan woarde men oan kant set.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Heesselt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.0929,"rank":0.0377,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV009205","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Whoever is born with a caul can see the future. If the caul is buried at once, nothing is wrong.\nA woman keeps six cauls of children who died.","place":"Onstwedde","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"TM 2901","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44560","original":"Mit helm geboorn.\nKiek, wel mit helm geboorn is, kan veuroet zain; hai wordt spuikkieker. As de helm onmiddelk in de grond stopt wordt, is dr niks an de hand, man anders worden t bezundere mensn.\nEn leuft ais, dat dat nich zo mooi is.\nDou k in dainst was, kwam ik wol ais bie n vrouw in hoes, dai zes helms in de kaaste lign har. Dai wazzen van zes kinder, dai allemoal overleden warn; man de helms har t oal mens opbaargt. Zai wol ze mie wol ais zain loatn, man door har ik ja gain belang bie.\nt Wazzen dreuge vliezn. In de vörm van n haalve bolle.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV013104","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A corpse that lies unburied over a Sunday means another death within six weeks.","place":"Bellingwolde","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44380","original":"n Volksgeleuf was wieder, dat as ain liek n zundag overstun, dat er den binnen zes weekn weer ['n] staarfgeval komen zol.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CBAK0041","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Prediction that a child will not live long. The child indeed dies at the age of six.","place":"Broek in Waterland","prov":"N.-H.","year":1899,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/8638","original":"Grietje Holleman heeft tegen een broertje van een Broeker dame gezegd dat hij niet oud zou worden. Op zes-jarige leeftijd is hij overleden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","6 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":6},"on_success":{"chime":6,"digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.2223,"rank":0.3953,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBOEK305","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"Another ghost story tells of a lady in a white veil who comes through the wall between twelve and one o'clock. If anyone disturbs her rest, she wrings his neck. A strong man goes to the castle she haunts at night and destroys her for good.","place":"Driebergen-Rijsenburg","prov":"Utr.","year":1892,"code":"SINSAG 0301","initials":"M.R.v.d.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/34810","original":"Een Spookgeschiedenis\nEen spookgeschiedenis zooals deze is er nog een, waarin eene geheimzinnige witgesluierde Dame het spook is; welke eveneens tusschen 12 en 1 uur komt, maar door den muur heen in de slaapkamer en roept, (wanneer zij iemand in de kamer ziet, welke het spook dooden wil), met een holle, nare grafstem: \"Wie stoort hier mijn rust?\" Daarop loopt zij toornig op den bevenden man toe en draait hem den hals om; daarna verdwijnt zij weer door den muur, alhoewel er geen deur in is. Nu durft niemand meer te wagen op het kasteel een nacht te slapen; totdat er eindelijk een moedige sterken man komt, op 't slot des nachts gaat en de witte Dame voor altijd verdelgt...\n(Breedvoerig ken ik deze historie niet meer.)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ006515","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"Two white women haunt the Lytse Wei. People do not go past there in the dark.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16867","original":"Op 'e Lytse Wei spoeken twa wite wiven. Yn 't tsjuster doarsten se dêr net lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN009501","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"Encounter with a lady without a head; digging up three chests of treasure fails because the silence is broken.","place":"Diergaarde","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208983","original":"Juffrouw zonder kop.. De paardeknecht van de boerderij \"de Horst\"onder de gemeente Echt, kwam 's avonds eens van de kermis thuis. Hij was over de grens geweest op Gulichs gebied en keerde door de bossen van \"de Doort\" terug. Hij had rijkelijk veel gedronken, raakte de weg kwijt en besloot maar te gaan liggen en de volgende morgen af te wachten. Juist hoorde hij de torenklok van Echt twaalf uur slaan en daarop aansluitend sloeg de klok van Dieteren (Susteren) ook twaalf. Dus Driekus, de knecht telde 24 slage n \"Zo laat ben ik nog nooit thuisgekomen\", dacht hij, \"wat is het hier toch een gekke boel, zowel met de weg als met de tijd.\"\nNauwelijks was hij ingeslapen of hij werd wakker door een vreemd geluid. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ053309","role":"inside","render":{"description":"One night a man suddenly sees two white women. The two women sit down on his cart. The man becomes so frightened that he quickly runs off.","place":"Ons Belang","prov":"Utr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25339","original":"Hjir ien út 'e Harkema ried us mei de boerewein op in nacht nei Readskuorre ta. Doe seach er dêr ynienen twa wite froulju foar him. Hy ried dêr mei de hynders lyk op yn.\nDoe kommen dy beide froulju yn 't wyt by him op 'e wein.\nHy woarde sa binaud, dat hy sette sokken en naeide út.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 12.","12 — 2 — 3."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"f49b6b07e38cc148","accepted_hashes":["14d00cdfe8f2791000ca7966bbd20b524114e142d471521f8c053e25e849550d"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2302,"rank":0.7455,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ029903","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A bridal couple is on the way to the town hall when the bridegroom-to-be suddenly bites a piece out of his bride's apron. The man is a werewolf; the girl breaks it off at once.","place":"Kûkherne","prov":"Fr.","year":1953,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21918","original":"It gebeurde us dat twa jonge lju yn 'e wein sieten nei 't gemeentehûs ta. Hja soenen dy deis trouwe. Underweis yn 'e wein byt de man har in stik út 'e skelk. Hy wie in wjerwolf. Hja makke it fuort út.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CBOEK477","role":"member","render":{"description":"On a wager, a farmhand must show that he dares to throw the spit into the Witte Wieven (white women) pit. He throws it and challenges the witte wief (white woman), who chases him. The farmhand jumps over the lower half of the door, horse and all. The witte wief throws the spit, which sticks in the middle post of the door.","place":"Bathmen","prov":"Ov.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"J.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/39631","original":"In de buurtschap Loo, op het erve Noever ging men een weddenschap aan met een knecht, dat hij het spit niet durfde gooien in de Witte-wieven-kuul; deze bevond zich daar ergens in de buurt. Hij sprong te paard en joeg derwaarts, aldaar smeet hij het spit in de kuil met de woorden:\n\nWit wieven wit\nHier breng ik oe een spit\n(of: Wat heb ie'j op oe spit?)\n\nDaarop had het wit wief gezegd:\n\nA'j zoo lang wacht\nDak mien eene schoe toeknuppe\nEn de aander toerukke\nDan zal ie'j 't gebraad wezen.\n\nDe knecht rende toen in vliegenden vaart huiswaarts, achtervolgd door het wit wief en voor de achterdeur gekomen, was de bovendeur los en de onderdeur dicht, maar het paard was nogal vlug en sprong over de onderdeur. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST279","role":"member","render":{"description":"A farmhand brings the spit to the Witte Wieven (white women). One of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost). The Witte Wief could not run faster because she had trouble with one of her shoes.","place":"Tilligte","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":null,"initials":"B.R.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13623","original":"Door ouden wordt nog van de Wit Wieve verteld, die alleen kwaadaardig waren, wanneer ze getergd werden. Zo wordt verteld dat een boerenknecht eens het spit bracht naar de plaats, waar zij woonden. Hij werd door eene der witte wieve achtervolgd, doch hem niet kon inhalen, omdat ze in de haast maar een schoen had kunnen aantrekken. Toen de knecht het huis binnenvluchtte, wierp ze hem met een bijl achterna, die in de steil (deurpost) terecht kwam.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_15_003","role":"member","render":{"description":"About the existence of witte wieven (white women) and the spit in the doorpost.","place":"Geesteren","prov":"Ov.","year":1979,"code":null,"initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128566","original":"H.E.: Van de witn wiew he’j doar wa mangs van heurd?\nVr.Vr.: Van de witn wiew is ok niks van woar.\nH.E.: Nee, mer te geet ok um t verhaal, he. Joa he’j hier nog zonnen beuld, zonnen witn wievnbeuld. Ne, nee, nee (door elkaar heen gepraat, ze zijn het met elkaar niet eens)\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Wat hadn ze bie ouns ok zegd, oh jee no valt mie t kenneke in zee Dat stun nog moal vuur joarn in de Twentse kraant. Als ik t met ene schoen had vastgebondn, gevondn als de ander gebondn.\nA.Ve.: ... t spit nog in n stiel van n nienduur nog zitn.\nF.Ve.: t Spit brengn.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Kûkherne belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0901,"rank":0.7966,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ005402","role":"card","render":{"description":"The narrator's father was once going back from Sânbulten to Zwaagwesteinde at one o'clock at night. In the Zwagerbosch he suddenly saw five women standing there wearing pointed caps and long white skirts. There was not a breath of wind, yet the plumes of the caps waved to and fro. He was frightened to death and went to old Bearn's farm. When they went to look together, the women were gone.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16510","original":"Heit hat us in kear nei de Sânbulten to praten west. Om ien ûre yn 'e nacht gong er werom nei de Westerein ta. Op Sânbulten moest er oer 't spoar en sa kom er troch Sweagerbosk. 't Wie blêdstil en moai sacht waer. Der wie neat dat him forroerde.\nDoe seach heit dêr yn Sweagerbosk ynienen fiif froulju stean, allegear mei in puntmûtse op en lange wite rokken oan. Hoewol it blêdstil waer wie, waeiden de tûfen [fan] de puntmûtsen al mar hinne en wer. Heit wie deabinaud. Hy gong nei âlde Bearn op 't hiem en kloppe dêr op 'e achterdoar. Hy kloppe Bearn der út. Hy fortelde Bearn mei in triljend lûd hwat er sjoen hie. Doe gong Bearn mei him om nei dy froulju to sjen. Mar doe wie der net ien mear. Doe't heit yn 'e Westerein oankom, trille er noch.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ034801","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte juffers (white maidens) haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22700","original":"Us mem biwearde, to Aldegea spoeke it op in smel reedtsje by Jan Japiksma. Dêr wie in boskje mei in gracht der omhinne. Dêr spoeken wite juffers.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070a","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a crossroads near Jistrum it was haunted at night. One evening, after a party, one of Durk Jaringa's sons passed that crossroads and saw a white figure floating just in front of him. He ran head over heels back to Jistrum. Later some others took him home past the crossroads, but there was no longer anything to be seen of the figure.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12146","original":"Wite juffers\nTe Jistrum, oan 'e noardkant, dêr krúst de Spoekloane de wei dy't fan Jistrum nei de Grinzerstrjitwei rint. Op dat krúspunt doogde it lang net. Dêr gong wol ris in wite gestalte dwers oer de wei, flak foar de minsken lâns. Ik wit noch wol, dat ien fan Durk Jaringa's jonges-se wennen oan 'e grutte strjitwei- de jûnes nei 'De Lindeboom' yn Jistrum west hie - sa hiet de jachtweide fan Jan van der Schors. It hie der tige gesellich west, hy hie in slokje dronke en om in oere of tsien, alven sette er op hûs yn. Hy kaam dêr op dy fjouwersprong en dêr gong dy wite gestalte flak foar him lâns. Hy waard sa kjel, dat hy stode hals oer de kop wer nei Justrum ta en dêr fûn er andergeloks noch lju yn 'e herberch. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ZEEUW047","role":"card","render":{"description":"At night a white woman appears and disappears into a well. After the well is filled in, she no longer appears.","place":"Yerseke","prov":"Zl.","year":1923,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.D.v.O.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38973","original":"Witte Juffers\nOok te Ierseke verscheen de Witte Vrouw op een stuk grond tusschen Lepel- en Mosselstraat. Later heeft men uit de voorwerpen die daar gevonden zijn, kunnen nagaan dat dit opgehoogde terrein in de oudheid als kerkhof heeft gediend, en vermoedelijk ook een vluchtheuvel was.\nVele omwonenden hebben haar, in het holle van den nacht, gezien. Ze verdween dan altijd in een diepe welput. Na het dichten van de put, kwam de witte vrouw niet weer. Ze had rust gevonden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ063612","role":"card","render":{"description":"In Almelo they have witte wijven (white women) and a beautiful woman haunts the place. I heard that when I was buying horses there.","place":"Soesterberg","prov":"Utr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27090","original":"In Almelo hebben ze witte wiven. En daar spookt ook nog een mooie vrouw om. Ik heb het daar wel eens gehoord toen ik daar peerden kocht.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ018012","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three white ladies, sisters, always haunt a haunted spot. Later that place was also said to be called the 'Susterwei'.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20251","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Garyp. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c6","object":"window","text":"Garyp"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c6","word":"three","stained":"c6"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.8646,"rank":0.9828,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBOEK091","role":"top","render":{"description":"A young man is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1894,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"J.F.C.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13127","half":"top"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST027","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"At a birthday party they do not let him leave. Suddenly a wolfskin falls down the chimney into the fire. It burns and the young man is freed.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ZEEUW181","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When they threw the skin into the oven, he came running up screaming, but when it was burnt, he was glad to be rid of it. They had found out that he was the werewolf by throwing a blue apron to the wolf; the next day the farmhand had blue threads between his teeth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST198","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When the walker comes home, his family knows at once from the nosebleed that he has carried a werewolf. The victims of a werewolf are mostly poachers or smugglers who ply their trade at night.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0801"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBOEK490","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A bearskin comes down the chimney, which he has to put on and then go through the village at night. His father, who is now dead, used to have to do it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"VVUNL315","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Tis the smith drags the rugplakker (back-clinger), holding it by the legs, to Sjaak's café, where he bangs open the door and quick Peerke gives the monster a slash, so that blood streams from its head and there stands the farmhand of the \"Beese\" (a farm in the area), who runs off at once, after which nothing more was heard of the werewolf.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0801"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"LYST236","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"While the unfortunate man is playing cards, everyone stays seated until it strikes twelve. The bewitched man grows more and more nervous, but everyone simply stays put. On the stroke of twelve the werewolf's skin rolls in down the chimney and is burnt in the fireplace amid loud cheering. The man is released from the spell.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"LYST024","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"His friends want to play a joke on him and shut all the windows and doors. After half an hour the man changes into a werewolf. His friends flee, but a brave thatcher stabs the werewolf. The man is now released.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0822"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CBOEK091","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the young man's teeth. Werewolves always wear a band around their waist. The farmer the young man works for burns the band. The werewolf still tries to get into the fire, but he is held back. When the band has burned, the young man is an ordinary person again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CJ017409","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man quickly makes off, but his wife follows him. She sees him tearing the skirt with his teeth; foam is around his mouth. The man confesses that he is a werewolf and had to bite into a cloth, because otherwise he would have had to attack a person. The woman calls off the wedding at once.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"TINNEV032","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The farmhand lies on his back with his mouth open, and at a certain moment a mole crawls out of it. The mole goes after the cows in the meadow and then crawls back. The farmhand stretches and gets up. But then he has to vomit. The day labourer sees him throwing up blood. The farmhand goes home and the day labourer goes to sow the grass. Later the farmer says that a calf has gone missing. When the farmhand has died, the coffin is so heavy that nobody can lift it. The minister cannot do anything about it either. They fetch the priest. He ties a rope to the coffin and pulls it from its place. Now the coffin can be lifted and taken to the churchyard.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0804"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1308","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"My grandfather once told me that a fisherman was attacked by a werewolf, but when he beat it up and stabbed it with a knife, the man went around in bandages the next day.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0822"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"BROUWERS002507","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A werewolf comes at the girl, who throws the box at it. The werewolf disappears, the boy returns.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘handkerchief’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0823. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c9"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c9"],"stack":["c1","c9"]},"found_card":{"card":"c9"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2475,"rank":0.7798,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015102","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"An impatient, rough farmer wants a large piece of land ploughed before evening. The farmhand refuses and tells the farmer he can take his proposal to the devil. The farmer takes this literally and enlists the devil's help. The next morning the land is ploughed. His dealings with the devil cost the farmer dearly: on his deathbed he was fetched by the devil.","place":"Hurdegaryp","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19770","original":"Der wie in boer, dat wie in forwoesteling. Hy wie altyd gleonhastich en net in arbeider dy't it by him úthâlde koe. Op in kear hied er wer in arbeider, doe moest der ploege wurde. It wie al let yn 'e joun en it wie ûnmooglik dy greate hoeke lân foar de nacht noch to ploeijen. Dat de arbeider sei tsjin 'e boer: \"Freegje de duvel, dat dy it docht.\" De boer sei: \"Dat dog ik\" en hy die it ek.\nDe oare moarns wie it stik lân ploege.\nMar hy hat it sûr bikeapje matten. Doe't er op syn stjerbêd lei, hat de duvel him helle.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"member","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":null,"initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ENGELS000115","role":"member","render":{"description":"Werewolf leaps on people in the evening; as a helper with work; transformation into a werewolf by putting on a hidden coat, release after the coat is burned.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/57969","original":"Weerwolven:\nMannen, die wat laat op de baan waren, werden, vooral in donkere, stormachtige nachten soms besprongen door de weerwolf. Dit spookdier met gloeiende ogen sprong hen op de rug, en klemde zich met de voorpoten om hun nek. Ze bleven zich als een zware last aan de verschrikte man klemmen totdat hij ergens een huis bereikte. In de Broekbeemd, tussen Onder-Eijndt en Zandberg, stond ergens een holle eiken knot of poesjt. Er was een man, die als weerwolf bekend werd. Hij had een aparte jas; als hij deze aantrok werd hij weerwolf. Na zijn nachtelijke tochten verborg hij deze jas in die holle “poesjt”. Zijn buurlui ontdekten dit, en staken de “poesjt” met de jas in brand. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"member","render":{"description":"A tenant farmer finds out that a young shepherd on his farm is probably a werewolf. He sends him away for a day, and he and his farmhands discover a wolfskin in a hollow willow. They set fire to it at home. The shepherd then comes back at a furious pace and tries to grab his skin back. When he fails, the shepherd flees to the hollow tree and is never seen again.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43423","original":"Het weerwolfsvel verbrand\n\nBij de pachter van de boerderij bij het kasteel Geusselt onder Amby diende eens een scheper, een klein manneke, dat de naam had een weerwolf te zijn. 's Nachts was hij nooit in bed te vinden, maar 's morgens lag hij er weer in. De knechts van de hoeve hadden dat al dikwijls bemerkt.\nWijl dit zo opvallend was, werd zijn doen en laten gedurig bespied en zo bemerkte men dan ook dat hij, wanneer hij 's avonds uit zijn bed kroop, naar een weide ging, waar heel eenzaam een grote holle wilg stond. Daar verdween hij iedere keer in.\nOm het fijne van de zaak te achterhalen stuurde de pachter hem op zekere namiddag naar een dorp, dat meer dan drie uur van de hoeve lag, om daar koeien te kopen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Hurdegaryp belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.079,"rank":0.6923,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"TINNEV043","role":"card","render":{"description":"Two men are cutting grass stalks when one asks the other whether he would like to see him for once. Immediately a wolf is lying in the grass. The man never wants to work with the other again.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22389","original":"30.\nOp een andere kier vroeg Dorus aan Peter, toe ze aan 't smele sui'je ware: \"Wi'j um is zien?\" Medeen derop lei een grote wolf ien 't gres. Peter wol van toe af aan de niet meer met Dorus op uut.","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ039818","role":"door","render":{"description":"One of seven successive sons is a werewolf.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23535"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST189","role":"card","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c4","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6696,"rank":0.25,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV009505","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At midnight the ghost of a murdered person haunts and blood spatters up at the place of the murder. A boy then does not dare look over his right shoulder.","place":"Stadskanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44586"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV015701","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Late in the evening a man notices that the back door of the cowshed is open and hears rumbling that does not come from the cows. The farmer says that a woman who was murdered there haunts now and then.","place":"Musselkanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45797","original":"Mien voader kon kwoad zain en hef mie door veul van verteld. Hai dainde as jongkerel bie de boer. Op n keer kwam e wat loat in hoes. Dan gung e deur de achterdeure van de dele, umdat andere deurn dicht zatn. As hai dan dele opstapt, heurt hai n geluud, man zug niks. \n“Kou lös”, denkt e. Hai zöcht n schienvat op en gait de baistn bie langs. Man nee heur, alles is rustig. \n Zeker wat verbeeld, zo denkt hai. Nich laank loater overkomp hum t zulfde; weer gestommel op dele en t binnen gain koi-en, dai t doun. \nNon wait hai nich meer, wat e door van denkn mout. Wol wait hai wizze, dat e nooit meer deur de baanderdeure wil. \nAnder dag under t eetn proot hai dr over mit de boer. Dai zeg eerst niks. …","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ105507","role":"variant","render":{"description":"At night one can sometimes see the white apparition of a murdered woman.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37578","original":"Mem fortelde, hjir yn 'e Pein hat in huzinge stien mei in gracht der by. Dêr is alris in frommeske formoarde woarn. Sûnt seach men dêr nachts in frou yn 't wyt troch de gracht hinne rinnen. Dat wie dat formoarde frommeske.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Groningen a time of day was mentioned: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1965.","That card names a time of day. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"f49b6b07e38cc148","accepted_hashes":["463c1bd859fa85db29b438a6569ed17dab9c3ce433fa6444dbf24768bc2b5fb2","a0a0af5512afa7f90915675e9d75533b6cb07508d105e7e8fc1e4456003f93ae","aadf8b3c1d8478fd66a7bf4a581027ea8cb1c66f1efb1990f1436c96fb73cb4b","da1084f88885c6e462ddf58b0d8863988e87bf1b58081c43ad67136bc42e908a","fa9f5877fae1bf93158536dc873e0a6b0d5c3a0d205f97c01187d2a98ffa3f6f"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.212,"rank":0.7143,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015603","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A fisherman sees a lady in white clothes and decides to follow her. But the wit wief (white woman) vanishes as quickly as she appeared.","place":"Broeksterwâld","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19893","original":"Douwe syn broer Anne Feddema hie to fiskjen west. Hy hie nei 't tichtset ta west en farde de Lyts út wei werom de kant nei de brêge út. Doe kom der in juffer oan yn sniewite klean. Hy tocht: Ik wol wite hwer't dy keart, dat hy hie 't eech net fan har ôf. Doe't er oan har ta wie, died er de fêstsetter yn 'e kant en krekt doe't er dat die, wie de wite juffer fuort.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"DYKFRIES2153","role":"member","render":{"description":"A glowing foal haunted the Leppedijk. A farm girl had stayed in the village until late and had to go home alone. When she was warned about the ghost foal, she claimed she would put her garter in its mouth and ride it home. But when she actually met the animal, she was terrified and ran home.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69329","original":"Op den Leppedijk, niet ver van Oldeboorn, spookte voorheen een gloeiend veulen. Eene boerenmeid was op zekeren avond wat laat in het dorp gebleven en toen haar gezegd werd, dat het veulen haar wel kon ontmoeten, zei ze, dat zij hem dan haar kouseband in den bek zou doen en op hem naar huis rijden. Maar toen zij, op den weg gekomen, het veulen eensklaps vóór zich zag met den bek wijd opengesperd, toen liep zij zoo hard zij kon om tehuis te komen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"DYKFRIES2191","role":"member","render":{"description":"If someone walked there at night, he might unexpectedly see a white foal racing past him at full speed, after which it suddenly vanished.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69795","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"DYKFRIES2156","role":"member","render":{"description":"A farmer from Westdongeradeel regularly encountered a plaaggeest (tormenting spirit). The animal always walked home with him but did him no further harm. The farmer made sure he could always offer the animal a piece of rye bread. His maidservant claimed she would be braver and that if she met the animal, she would ride home on it. When she once met the animal, it put its front paws on her shoulders, so that the maid was forced to carry the animal's weight on her way home.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":null,"initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69345","original":"In Westdongeradeel woonde weleer een boer die veel last had van een plaagbeest. Was de man 's avonds bij duister op weg naar zijn huis, dan kwam hem meest altijd zulk een spookdier op zijde. Het vergezelde hem tot aan zijn erf. Eens zelfs was het meegegaan over het bruggetje, dat aan den weg over de gracht lag. Maar dat was dan ook alles; eigenlijk kwaad deed het hem niet. Hij zorgde altijd een stuk roggebrood bij zich te hebben, waarop hij 't beest dan onthaalde. Dit scheen daar smaak in te vinden, nam het gretig aan en liet den boer ongedeerd. Maar de man was toch altijd ontsteld als hij in huis kwam. Zijne dienstmeid vond dit wel wat dwaas en schroomde ook niet voor hare meening uit te komen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Broeksterwâld belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1273,"rank":0.375,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST162","role":"top","render":{"description":"In the old days people said you should not walk in the middle of the road after dark, or you ran the risk of being thrown to the side of the road or into the verge. It also happened that people were followed by a dog that kept walking along until they reached home. In wooded areas","place":"Oranjewoud","prov":"Fr.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13413","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ010112","role":"half","render":{"description":"The beast is very big and yellow, and it flaps its ears. It passes right by the man and stays with him for a while. The man thinks it was a plaagbeest (tormenting beast).","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST162","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"two fiery eyes would sometimes stare at people. Those eyes were the \"Evil One\", always lying in wait.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333","stain":"two"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ080711","role":"half","render":{"description":"In the middle of the road stood a very big dog that would not let him pass. That was a plaagbeest (a phantom beast that harasses people). The man went back again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0256"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ018108","role":"half","render":{"description":"When the rats ran around, you could hear the money jingle. When the place was later demolished, they found all the money. It was a haunted place.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP280","role":"half","render":{"description":"They brought misfortune to anyone who tried to chase them away. Such chained dogs also used to appear in the area around Broekhuizen, Broekhuizenvorst, Blitterswijk, Wanssum, Geysteren, Maashees and Venray. In Blitterswijk it was called the 'patershond' (friar's dog), and people preferred to keep well away from it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ060905","role":"half","render":{"description":"When Schopper, the director of the Wilhelminahoeve, hears this he does not believe it, but he has to admit she is right when they see it themselves too.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0477"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The machine stops in mid-sentence. The rest finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0333. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c3","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c3"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1","word":"two","stained":"c3"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
